; print must keep the commodity of a zero balance assignment: `= $0`
; printed as a bare `= 0` cannot be read back for an account that
; holds more than one commodity.

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash    $10
    Assets:Cash    5 EUR
    Equity

2024/01/02 Spend dollars
    Assets:Cash    = $0
    Expenses:Misc

2024/01/03 Spend euros
    Assets:Cash    = 0 EUR
    Expenses:Misc

test print
2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash                                  $10
    Assets:Cash                                5 EUR
    Equity

2024/01/02 Spend dollars
    Assets:Cash                                 = $0
    Expenses:Misc

2024/01/03 Spend euros
    Assets:Cash                              = 0 EUR
    Expenses:Misc
end test

test bal
